the left-hand side of this equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/52cb8ea4/img_009_03113042.png" alt="3 x plus 3 y, equals negative 5"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from miscalculating <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/52cb8ea4/img_010_b06e1caa.png" alt="4 minus 9 "></span> as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/52cb8ea4/img_011_140a0460.png" alt="negative 13"></span>. Choice C is incorrect and may result from miscalculating <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/52cb8ea4/img_012_b06e1caa.png" alt="4 minus 9 "></span> as 5. Choice D is incorrect and may result from adding 9 to 4 instead of subtracting 9 from 4.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
