e64,\" alt=\"the ordered pair x comma y \"></span></span> is the solution to the system of equations above, what is the value of&nbsp;<span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x plus 3 y\"></span>&nbsp;</span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 13\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 5\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p>5</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p>13</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. Subtracting the second equation, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"4 x minus 8 y, equals 9\"></span>, from the first equation, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"7 x minus 5 y, equals 4\"></span>, results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 7 x minus 5 y, close parenthesis, minus, open parenthesis, 4 x minus 8 y, close parenthesis, equals, 4 minus 9\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"7 x minus 5 y, minus 4 x, plus 8 y, equals 5\"></span>. Combining like terms on the left-hand side of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x plus 3 y, equals negative 5\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from miscalculating <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"4 minus 9 \"></span> as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 13\"></span>. Choice C is incorrect and may result from miscalculating <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"4 minus 9 \"></span> as 5. Choice D is incorrect and may result from adding 9 to 4 instead of subtracting 9 from 4.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959624,"updateDate":1691007959624}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959624, 1691007959624),
    ($SATQ$53487897$SATQ$, $SATQ$940b3aad-7c94-4109-8fe4-ef6351e23009$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The relationship between two variables, <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>, is linear. For every increase in the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> increases by <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>. When the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math>. Which equation represents this relationship?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"6d79027d-0082-4e35-a69c-c6ce92e4afc4","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 x plus 18\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>18</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"99d623bb-b04f-4602-9d96-6f885d8e0b1f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 x plus 8\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"74bbdc66-401e-41aa-9210-57d6faf61c74","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"23b01717-da26-4313-87a3-9f5066e74a63","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 3 x plus 26\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>26</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["74bbdc66-401e-41aa-9210-57d6faf61c74"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the relationship between <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is linear. An equation representing a linear relationship can be written in the form <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> is the slope and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of the relationship in the <em>xy</em>-plane. It&rsquo;s given that for every increase in the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> increases by <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>. The slope of a line can be expressed as the change in <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> over the change in <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>. Thus, the slope, <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math>, of the line representing this relationship can be expressed as <math alttext="eight oneths"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="y equals 8 x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>8</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. It's also given that when the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="y equals 8 x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>8</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="18 equals 8 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis plus b"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, or <math alttext="18 equals 16 plus b"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Subtracting <math alttext="16"><mn>16</mn>
</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext="2 equals b"><mrow>
	<mn>2</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>b</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="y equals 8 x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>8</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="y equals 8 x plus 2"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>8</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>2</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the equation <math alttext="y equals 8 x plus 2"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>8</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>2</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> represents this relationship.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> increases by <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>, and when the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="22"><mn>22</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> increases by <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>, and when the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="12"><mn>12</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> increases by <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>, and when the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="32"><mn>32</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"53487897","external_id":"940b3aad-7c94-4109-8fe4-ef6351e23009","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"e8beed61-bb7e-47a2-a781-88c4728ad36d","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.B.","skill_desc":"Linear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The relationship between two variables, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, is linear. For every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>. When the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>. Which equation represents this relationship?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"6d79027d-0082-4e35-a69c-c6ce92e4afc4","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 x plus 18\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>18</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"99d623bb-b04f-4602-9d96-6f885d8e0b1f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 x plus 8\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"74bbdc66-401e-41aa-9210-57d6faf61c74","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"23b01717-da26-4313-87a3-9f5066e74a63","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 3 x plus 26\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>26</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["74bbdc66-401e-41aa-9210-57d6faf61c74"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the relationship between <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is linear. An equation representing a linear relationship can be written in the form <math alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> is the slope and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of the relationship in the <em>xy</em>-plane. It&rsquo;s given that for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>. The slope of a line can be expressed as the change in <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> over the change in <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>. Thus, the slope, <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math>, of the line representing this relationship can be expressed as <math alttext=\"eight oneths\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It's also given that when the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"18 equals 8 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis plus b\"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"18 equals 16 plus b\"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn>\n</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"2 equals b\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the equation <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> represents this relationship.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, and when the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, and when the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, and when the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"32\"><mn>32</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357388,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"53487897","skill_cd":"H.B.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Linear functions","createDate":1730147357388,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"","external_id":"940b3aad-7c94-4109-8fe4-ef6351e23009","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"e8beed61-bb7e-47a2-a781-88c4728ad36d","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 x plus 18\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>18</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"6d79027d-0082-4e35-a69c-c6ce92e4afc4"},{"content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 x plus 8\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"99d623bb-b04f-4602-9d96-6f885d8e0b1f"},{"content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"74bbdc66-401e-41aa-9210-57d6faf61c74"},{"content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 3 x plus 26\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>26</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"23b01717-da26-4313-87a3-9f5066e74a63"}],"externalid":"940b3aad-7c94-4109-8fe4-ef6351e23009","keys":["74bbdc66-401e-41aa-9210-57d6faf61c74"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the relationship between <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is linear. An equation representing a linear relationship can be written in the form <math alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> is the slope and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of the relationship in the <em>xy</em>-plane. It&rsquo;s given that for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>. The slope of a line can be expressed as the change in <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> over the change in <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>. Thus, the slope, <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math>, of the line representing this relationship can be expressed as <math alttext=\"eight oneths\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It's also given that when the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"18 equals 8 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis plus b\"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"18 equals 16 plus b\"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn>\n</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"2 equals b\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>b</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the equation <math alttext=\"y equals 8 x plus 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> represents this relationship.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, and when the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, and when the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a relationship where for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>, and when the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"32\"><mn>32</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The relationship between two variables, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, is linear. For every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> increases by <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>. When the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>. Which equation represents this relationship?</p>","type":"mcq","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1730147357388,"updateDate":1730147357388}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357388, 1730147357388),
    ($SATQ$535fa6e6$SATQ$, $SATQ$9040ee10-4498-4a27-b92f-5181148b3e11$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$52547983-af73-41c2-ac5a-587286567fb9$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Davio bought some potatoes and celery. The potatoes cost <math alttext="dollar sign 0.69"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.69</mn></math> per pound, and the celery cost <math alttext="dollar sign 0.99"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.99</mn></math> per pound. If Davio spent <math alttext="dollar sign 5.34"><mo>$</mo><mn>5.34</mn></math> in total and bought twice as many pounds of celery as pounds of potatoes, how many pounds of celery did Davio buy?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"0fe3bb42-90bf-4f8a-97cb-1a4b56ce415b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"89227a25-10a3-45e2-ab49-e1781c216878","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2.5\"><mn>2.5</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"83b61fe4-c635-4447-a02f-112f7970362d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2.67\"><mn>2.67</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"92e62a2f-1170-4c5e-b6ac-a913b72a6cbf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["92e62a2f-1170-4c5e-b6ac-a913b72a6cbf"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. Let <math alttext="p"><mi>p</mi></math> represent the number of pounds of potatoes and let <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> represent the number of pounds of celery&nbsp;that Davio bought. It&rsquo;s given that potatoes cost <math alttext="dollar sign 0.69"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.69</mn></math> per pound and celery costs <math alttext="dollar sign 0.99"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.99</mn></math> per pound. If Davio spent <math alttext="dollar sign 5.34"><mo>$</mo><mn>5.34</mn></math> in total, then the equation <math alttext="0.69 p plus 0.99 c equals 5.34"><mn>0.69</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.34</mn></math> represents this situation. It&rsquo;s also given that Davio bought twice as many pounds of celery as pounds of potatoes; therefore, <math alttext="c equals 2 p"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></math>. Substituting <math alttext="2 p"><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></math> for <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> in the equation <math alttext="0.69 p plus 0.99 c equals 5.34"><mn>0.69</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.34</mn></math> yields <math alttext="0.69 p plus 0.99 left parenthesis 2 p right parenthesis equals 5.34"><mn>0.69</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5.34</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="0.69 p plus 1.98 p equals 5.34"><mn>0.69</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1.98</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.34</mn></math>, or <math alttext="2.67 p equals 5.34"><mn>2.67</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.34</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="2.67"><mn>2.67</mn></math> yields <math alttext="p equals 2"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Substituting&nbsp;<math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math alttext="p"><mi>p</mi></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="c equals 2 p"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="c equals 2 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="c equals 4"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Therefore, Davio bought&nbsp;<math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> pounds of celery.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of pounds of potatoes, not the number of pounds of celery, Davio bought.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"535fa6e6","external_id":"9040ee10-4498-4a27-b92f-5181148b3e11","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"52547983-af73-41c2-ac5a-587286567fb9","uId":"fb74942b-cd3e-4a8a-938d-7df8674c4ed5","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>Davio bought some potatoes and celery. The potatoes cost <math alttext=\"dollar sign 0.69\"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.69</mn></math> per pound, and the celery cost <math alttext=\"dollar sign 0.99\"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.99</mn></math> per pound. If Davio spent <math alttext=\"dollar sign 5.34\"><mo>$</mo><mn>5.34</mn></math> in total and bought twice as many pounds of celery as pounds of potatoes, how many pounds of celery did Davio buy?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"0fe3bb42-90bf-4f8a-97cb-1a4b56ce415b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"89227a25-10a3-45e2-ab49-e1781c216878","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2.5\"><mn>2.5</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"83b61fe4-c635-4447-a02f-112f7970362d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2.67\"><mn>2.67</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"92e62a2f-1170-4c5e-b6ac-a913b72a6cbf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["92e62a2f-1170-4c5e-b6ac-a913b72a6cbf"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. Let <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> represent the number of pounds of potatoes and let <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> represent the number of pounds of celery&nbsp;that Davio bought. It&rsquo;s given that potatoes cost <math alttext=\"dollar sign 0.69\"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.69</mn></math> per pound and celery costs <math alttext=\"dollar sign 0.99\"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.99</mn></m