    ($SATQ$5ab9903f$SATQ$, $SATQ$657150dc-4949-4ed3-afe8-a00d56bf8642$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in one variable$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The cost to rent a bus from Company X is <math alttext="dollar sign 950"><mo>$</mo><mrow><mn>950</mn></mrow></math> for the first <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> hours and an additional <math alttext="dollar sign 50"><mo>$</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow></math> per hour for each hour after the first <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> hours. If the total cost to rent the bus from Company X for <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> hours, where <math alttext="t greater than 3"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>, is <math alttext="dollar sign 1,150"><mo>$</mo><mrow><mn>1,150</mn></mrow></math>, which equation represents this situation?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"cc2f39ca-2bec-4d28-9733-8e5c964a76c0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"950 left parenthesis t minus 3 right parenthesis plus 50 t equals 1,150\"><mrow><mn>950</mn></mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1,150</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"8254c7aa-903b-499c-abcc-e664da606c34","content":"<p><math alttext=\"950 left parenthesis 3 t right parenthesis plus 50 t equals 1,150\"><mrow><mn>950</mn></mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1,150</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"33e15886-2509-4f61-9e49-b655798adb78","content":"<p><math alttext=\"950 plus 50 left parenthesis t minus 3 right parenthesis equals 1,150\"><mrow><mn>950</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1,150</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"203cd035-a37f-4ea5-ac6b-2c9ce25036ce","content":"<p><math alttext=\"950 plus 50 left parenthesis 3 t right parenthesis equals 1,150\"><mrow><mn>950</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1,150</mn></mrow></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["33e15886-2509-4f61-9e49-b655798adb78"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the cost to rent a bus is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="dollar sign 950"><mo>$</mo><mn>950</mn></math> for the first <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> hours and an additional <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="dollar sign 50"><mo>$</mo><mn>50</mn></math> per hour for each hour after the first <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> hours. It&rsquo;s also given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> represents the total number of hours and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t greater than 3"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Therefore, the number of additional hours after the first <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> hours can be represented by the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t minus 3"><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. The cost for these additional hours is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="dollar sign 50"><mo>$</mo><mn>50</mn></math> per hour, so the cost for the additional hours can be represented by the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="50 left parenthesis t minus 3 right parenthesis"><mn>50</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. The total cost can be calculated by adding the cost for the first <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> hours to the cost for the additional hours and can be represented by the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="950 plus 50 left parenthesis t minus 3 right parenthesis"><mn>950</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that the total cost to rent the bus from the company for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> hours is&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="dollar sign 1,150"><mo>$</mo><mn>1,150</mn></math>. Thus, the equation that represents this situation is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="950 plus 50 left parenthesis t minus 3 right parenthesis equals 1,150"><mn>950</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1,150</mn></math>.</p>
